{
  "title": "Selling Pieces of Wood",
  "difficulty": "Hard",
  "type": "matrix",
  "tags": [
    "Dynamic Programming",
    "Matrix"
  ],
  "description": "Find the maximum money earned by cutting a piece of wood of size m x n given a list of prices for specific height and width dimensions.",
  "target": 32,
  "pseudocode": "1. dp = new Array(m + 1).fill(0).map(() => new Array(n + 1).fill(0))\n2. for price in prices: dp[price.h][price.w] = price.p\n3. for i = 1 to m: for j = 1 to n:\n4.   for k = 1 to i/2: dp[i][j] = max(dp[i][j], dp[k][j] + dp[i-k][j])\n5.   for k = 1 to j/2: dp[i][j] = max(dp[i][j], dp[i][k] + dp[i][j-k])",
